'''Oriol Cardona i Ousmane''' (born 8 March 1991) is a Balboan politician who has served as mayor of [[Sant Cristòfor]] since 2025. A member of the [[Socialist Front of Balboa]] (FSB), he was elected in a snap election following the arrest of his predecessor, [[Núria Gomila i Renom]]. Before becoming mayor, he served first as a councillor for [[Pandao]] and later as a member of the [[Sant Cristòfor comarca assembly]].

Cardona i Ousmane's election marked the first time since the post-Guarantees period that Sant Cristòfor had elected a mayor outside the [[Balboan People's Party]] or the [[Liberal Party of Balboa|Liberal Party]]. His victory was widely interpreted as a rejection of the city's long-dominant two-party pattern and as a sign of public frustration with corruption allegations against the outgoing administration.

== Political career ==

=== Councillor for Pandao ===

Cardona i Ousmane entered local politics as a councillor for Pandao in 2012. During his time on the municipal council, he became associated with attention to day-to-day issues such as housing pressure, transport reliability, and waterfront access. He developed a reputation for constituency work, particularly on maintenance complaints, planning disputes, and local service issues.

=== Sant Cristòfor comarca assembly ===

In 2019, Cardona i Ousmane was elected to the Sant Cristòfor comarca assembly. There he became a more vocal figure, intervening on matters affecting multiple districts across the city rather than limiting himself to Pandao. His willingness to take up issues across Sant Cristòfor broadened his profile beyond his home district and helped establish him as a citywide political figure.

=== Mayoral election of 2025 ===

Cardona i Ousmane was elected mayor in 2025 after a snap election was called following the arrest of Gomila i Renom. His campaign emphasised social housing expansion, stronger tenants' rights, and support for waterfront workers affected by the city's transport and redevelopment policies.

His campaign was notable for extensive use of social media, repeated door-to-door canvassing, and a heavy focus on practical neighbourhood issues. Rather than centring his message on ideology, he framed the election as a choice about housing costs, transport reliability, and day-to-day municipal management.

One of his most prominent campaign pledges was the construction of the [[Line 1 extension to Barcelona]], a long-debated rapid transit project intended to improve links between [[Original (ciutat)|Original]] and the [[Barcelona (Sant Cristòfor)|Barcelona]] peninsula. He paired the project with a retraining programme for ferry workers affected by any decline in ridership on the [[Ferries de la Badia de Sant Cristòfor]].

=== Mayoralty ===

Since taking office, Cardona i Ousmane has presented himself as a hands-on administrator concerned with housing affordability, transport links, and waterfront redevelopment. His administration has been associated with the acceleration of major infrastructure works, a more interventionist approach to housing policy, and efforts to balance redevelopment with the interests of working-class waterfront communities.

=== Political style ===

Cardona i Ousmane's political style has been described as pragmatic and locally focused. As a councillor and later as a member of the comarca assembly, he cultivated a reputation for constituency service and for responding to immediate neighbourhood issues rather than advancing a highly ideological programme. His use of social media and direct canvassing was a central part of his campaigns, which emphasised accessibility, local responsiveness, and practical municipal administration.

== Background ==

Cardona i Ousmane was born in [[Pandao]], [[Barcelona (ciutat)|Barcelona]], to a family of dockworkers. He studied at the [[Universitat de Sant Cristòfor]] before entering local politics. Little has been published publicly about his early career, although he is identified in municipal and press coverage primarily through his political career and his role in the 2025 election.

He is not to be confused with the earlier Balboan cultural journalist [[Oriol Cardona]], who was active in the mid-20th century and is associated with ''[[La Voz del Istmo]]'' and the coining of the term ''[[istmo son]]''.

== Personal life ==

Cardona i Ousmane is married to [[Mireia Soler i Pons]].

